// lexdb over TDS: SQL Server 2025's REGEXP_ functions, checked against SQL Server 2025 (generated by
// tests/lexdb/gen_mssql.py --port 14331 --container lxl-mssql25 regexp from mssql_regexp_queries.txt;
// design/lexdb-new-features.md S1-S6): RE2's syntax as SQL Server reads it (leftmost-first; no ARE escapes), its flags
// (c, i, s, m; . not matching a newline and ^ $ at the ends by default; 19303 for others), REGEXP_LIKE a predicate only (156
// as a value), REGEXP_REPLACE every match by default, the arguments' errors (19301) and the patterns' (19300, 19307, 19308,
// 19309), REGEXP_MATCHES's rows (match_id, start_position, end_position, match_value, substring_matches as JSON text) and
// REGEXP_SPLIT_TO_TABLE's (value, ordinal), in FROM and APPLY; NULLs, empty input, 3,000 rows, an error in a later row.
// Each batch runs against lexdb with SET lexdb_batch = off and on: "same: " and the answer, or DIFFERENT and both.
